{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>Cast out this maidservant and her son.</b> For at her counsel the son committed the act of slandering, in order that <b>he might inherit</b> — therefore cast him out, for it is not just that <b>he should inherit</b> even a portion." "<b>For the son of the maidservant shall not inherit.</b> For he is not reckoned after you, since the offspring follows the defective one."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {0 "The Hebrew דִּבָּה traditionally refers to the slander/mockery reported in Genesis 21:9; rendered literally as 'slandering.'"}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:30:58.573303935Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}